Three commits on develop (#489's 1.17 is in): `feat(sdk): a prop fixed to a moby's joint, interface 1.18`, `feat(sdk): where a prop was drawn last, prop_frame (interface 1.18)` and `docs(sdk): a guide to props, on a joint too (interface 1.18)`.

## Why

A mod that adds a weapon draws the weapon's model as a prop (1.12), but could only pose it from its own tick:

- the pose lagged a frame behind the hero's animation, and the mod never saw his hand's matrix nor where the game puts its own pieces, so the model floated beside the hand;
- the game's own weapon could not be hidden for good: rac1 shows all the hero's held pieces again each tick (`update_hero_item_moby_flags`, from his own update, outside the moby updates and before the draw), so `moby_hide` on it lasted no frame;
- once the model sits in the hand, the mod still has to know where its muzzle is to start the shots there. rac1's held item moby keeps only the yaw and pitch of its joint, so that place is wrong as soon as the hero r

